  modelTitle: "Model and assumptions",
  modelBody: `<li><b>Parameters in the table</b> are measured on the simulated peaks with the Ph. Eur. 2.2.46 formulas: <code>k = (t_R − t_M)/t_M</code>, <code>α = k₂/k₁</code>, <code>N = 5.54·(t_R/w_h)²</code>, <code>R_s = 1.18·(t_R2 − t_R1)/(w_h1 + w_h2)</code>, <code>A_s = w_0.05/(2d)</code>, <code>S/N = 2H/h</code>. t<sub>R</sub> is the peak maximum.</li>
    <li><b>Retention:</b> LSS model, <code>log k = log k_w − S·φ</code>; k<sub>w</sub> and S refer to the selected modifier (switching ACN/MeOH only changes viscosity here). A negative S describes a HILIC system.</li>
    <li><b>Migration:</b> <code>dx/dt = u/(1+k(φ(x,t)))</code> integrated numerically; in gradient elution the composition at position x is <code>φ(t − t_D − x/u)</code>, t<sub>D</sub> = D/F, programme: initial isocratic → linear gradient → final isocratic.</li>
    <li><b>Hold-up time:</b> <code>V_M = ε_T·πr²L</code>, ε<sub>T</sub> = 0.65 (porous) or 0.50 (core-shell); <code>t_M = V_M/F</code>.</li>
    <li><b>Efficiency:</b> <code>h = A + B/ν + C·ν</code>, <code>ν = u·d_p/D_m</code>, <code>N_col = L/(h·d_p)</code>. Porous: A = 1.2, B = 2.0, C = 0.08; core-shell: A = 0.7, B = 1.6, C = 0.06.</li>
    <li><b>Peak shape:</b> Gaussian with <code>σ_t² = [t_M(1+k_e)]²/N_col + (σ_V² + V_inj²/12)/F²</code> convolved with an exponential tail (EMG). Tailing increases for basic compounds, especially on a phase without end-capping. The injection is a rectangular plug without on-column focusing; gradient band compression is neglected.</li>
    <li><b>Signal:</b> concentration-sensitive (UV) detector, peak area ∝ amount·V<sub>inj</sub>/F. White noise with standard deviation σ; h is the range of the blank noise over 5·w<sub>h</sub> (10 Hz sampling).</li>
    <li><b>Pressure:</b> <code>ΔP = Φ·η·L·u_s/d_p²</code>, Φ = 1500; viscosity of water–ACN and water–MeOH at 25 °C from an empirical approximation; the maximum is shown for gradients.</li>
    <li>Values are indicative – the model is for learning relationships, not for predicting a specific method.</li>`,
